WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
Here's a printed photo of a straight road,

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.300
lined with identical lamp posts.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.140
Slide a ruler across it.

4
00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.820
Not a single bump.

5
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.670
Completely flat.

6
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.310
Now shut one eye.

7
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.600
The road still stretches
away into the distance.

8
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.760
So how can a flat picture,
seen with just one eye,

9
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.710
still look deep?

10
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.470
In this mission, you'll discover that
the image on each retina is flat too.

11
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.200
Depth is something your brain works out.

12
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:33.290
Your eyes are a few centimetres apart,
so each gets a slightly different view.

13
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.850
You'll find out whether
that explains the photo,

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.150
and what your brain has
left when one eye is shut.

15
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: explain how a flat photo
can look deep when you shut one eye.
